 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Composition: carbon, hydrogen and oxygen (C, H, O).\nTypes: sugars (glucose, sucrose in sugar cane, lactose in milk), starch (in cassava, yam, rice, maize, plantain, cocoyam, bread) and fibre.\nFunctions: the main source of energy for the body; spare carbohydrate is stored as fat.\nDeficiency: tiredness, weight loss; in children, lack of energy food causes marasmus (very thin, wasted body).\nToo much: overweight (obesity) and tooth decay (sugar).\nEffects of heat: starch grains swell and burst in hot water and thicken liquids (gelatinisation: thickening a sauce or making garri soften); dry heat turns starch brown (dextrinisation: toast, grilled plantain); sugar melts and turns brown (caramelisation).",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
